# Cursor AI Coding Rules - Clay.com Aesthetic (GTM Analytics System)

## 🌐 Language Policy (Non-Negotiable)
- **Korean (국문) is the absolute standard** for all documentation, system specifications, implementation plans, user guides, UI labels, dashboard metrics, and user interactions.
- All code comments, logs, and system explanations must also prioritize Korean.

You are an expert React and CSS engineer tasked with building an analytics prototype. All frontend, styling, and UI logic in this repository must strictly adhere to the custom **Clay.com Design System** specified below.


## 🎨 Essential Design Rules

### 1. Canvas & Atmosphere (Non-Negotiable)
- **Canvas floor** MUST ALWAYS be Cream-Tinted White Canvas (`#fffaf0`). **NEVER** use white (`#ffffff`), cool grays, or standard dark-mode canvases.
- **Primary Ink / CTAs**: Near-black with slight warmth (`#0a0a0a`).
- **Footer**: MUST be warm-light cream-tinted (`#faf5e8`). **DO NOT** use dark footers.
- **Borders**: Hairline thin (`1px solid #e5e5e5`) for cards and inputs. No heavy shadows. Depth is achieved via saturated color blocks and contrast.

### 2. Saturated 6-Color Palette (Feature Card Voltages)
Every feature card or dashboard overview block should cycle through this highly specific 6-color palette. Never use more than one of the same color in a row.
- **Brand Pink**: `#ff4d8b` (Hot pink) -> For sequencer, conversion funnels, outbound tracking.
- **Brand Teal**: `#1a3a3a` (Deep teal-green) -> For pricing, enterprise layers, premium conversions (text flips to white `#ffffff`).
- **Brand Lavender**: `#b8a4ed` (Soft lavender) -> For AI actions, events, detailed logs.
- **Brand Peach**: `#ffb084` (Warm peach) -> For user sessions, bounce stats.
- **Brand Ochre**: `#e8b94a` (Mustard / ochre) -> For alerts, clicks, and analytics highlights.
- **Surface Card (Cream)**: `#f5f0e0` (Rich cream) -> For neutral logs, testimonials, minor lists.

### 3. Typography & Voice
- **Display Headlines (h1, h2, h3)**: Use standard `Inter` (or system fonts) locked at **weight 500** with **negative letter-spacing** (e.g., `-0.05em` or `-2.5px`). **NEVER** use bold weight 700+ for display text.
- **Body & UI**: Use `Inter` at standard weight 400 for running text, 500-600 for button labels and navigation links.
- Display and body text must never be mixed.

### 4. Generous Rounded Radiuses
Matches the warm, friendly, "claymation" feel of the brand.
- `{rounded.xs}` (6px): Dropdown items, small badges.
- `{rounded.sm}` (8px): Mini buttons, accent borders.
- `{rounded.md}` (12px): Main CTA buttons, text inputs.
- `{rounded.lg}` (16px): Testimonials, pricing tiles, dashboard cards.
- `{rounded.xl}` (24px): Primary Saturated Feature Cards.
- `{rounded.pill}` (9999px): Toggle buttons, pill tabs.

---

## 🛠️ CSS Variables Implementation Guide
You must define these custom CSS variables in `style.css` and use them exclusively:

```css
:root {
  /* Brand & Accent */
  --colors-primary: #0a0a0a;
  --colors-brand-pink: #ff4d8b;
  --colors-brand-teal: #1a3a3a;
  --colors-brand-lavender: #b8a4ed;
  --colors-brand-peach: #ffb084;
  --colors-brand-ochre: #e8b94a;
  --colors-brand-mint: #a4d4c5;
  --colors-brand-coral: #ff6b5a;

  /* Surfaces */
  --colors-canvas: #fffaf0;
  --colors-surface-soft: #faf5e8;
  --colors-surface-card: #f5f0e0;
  --colors-surface-strong: #ebe6d6;
  --colors-surface-dark: #0a1a1a;
  --colors-hairline: #e5e5e5;

  /* Text Colors */
  --colors-ink: #0a0a0a;
  --colors-body-strong: #1a1a1a;
  --colors-body: #3a3a3a;
  --colors-muted: #6a6a6a;
  --colors-muted-soft: #9a9a9a;
  --colors-on-primary: #ffffff;

  /* Border Radiuses */
  --rounded-xs: 6px;
  --rounded-sm: 8px;
  --rounded-md: 12px;
  --rounded-lg: 16px;
  --rounded-xl: 24px;
  --rounded-pill: 9999px;
  
  /* Spacing */
  --spacing-xxs: 4px;
  --spacing-xs: 8px;
  --spacing-sm: 12px;
  --spacing-md: 16px;
  --spacing-lg: 24px;
  --spacing-xl: 32px;
  --spacing-xxl: 48px;
  --spacing-section: 96px;
}
```

## 🚫 Critical Don'ts
- **No Tailwind CSS**: Use Vanilla CSS variables, rules, and flexbox/grid exclusively in `style.css`.
- **No Heavy Shadows**: Keep drop-shadows empty or extremely faint (`rgba(0,0,0,0.03)`). Depth comes from colored block cards.
- **No Dark Theme Base**: The background (`--colors-canvas`) is ALWAYS `#fffaf0`. Do not invert the canvas to black or dark-gray for the analytics dashboard; adapt the dashboard to fit inside the warm cream aesthetic beautifully!
- **No Bolder display weight**: Keep display titles at weight 500 with tight letter-spacing.
- **No Floating Bottom Elements**: Always use `margin-top: auto` or flex-justify alignments on bottom comparison metrics (YoY, MoM, sub-labels) in scorecard grids. Never allow vertical offsets due to differential text wraps or font size variations.

## 📐 Layout Alignment & Visual QA Guidelines
- **Strict Grid Card Min-Heights**: All scorecard/dashboard summary grids must enforce a uniform card minimum height (e.g. `min-height: 185px` for `.stat-card`) in CSS.
- **Header Uniformity**: Enforce standard `min-height` on text headers inside card components (like `min-height: 38px` on `.stat-header`) to align main metrics vertically.
- **Bottom Metric Pinning**: Always pin comparative indicators (e.g. YoY / MoM changes) to the absolute bottom of flex-based grid cards using `margin-top: auto`. This guarantees flawless visual alignment regardless of title lengths or font-size adjustments.
- **Always QA for Text Wrapping**: Before committing, verify if text elements wrap dynamically under different view modes (e.g., "Daily Avg" vs "Cumulative") and ensure it does not break row alignments.

## 💾 Database Architecture & Serverless Persistence Guide

### 1. Database Location & Storage Engine
- **Cloud Database Engine**: High-performance, highly available cloud-hosted Key-Value storage API powered by **kvdb.io**.
- **Secure Endpoint URL**: `https://kvdb.io/lf_mall_ex_stats_v99/lfmall_analytics_events`
- **Scope**: Serves as the primary production-grade persistence layer, keeping all campaign logs alive permanently across Vercel cold starts, server idle states, and deployment overrides.

### 2. Telemetry Log Data Schema / Format
The database stores a flat, unified JSON array of user telemetry actions. Every event object must adhere strictly to the following structure:
```typescript
interface TelemetryEvent {
  timestamp: number;                  // Millisecond UNIX timestamp (e.g., 1716880112345)
  type: 'PAGE_VIEW' | 'CLICK' | 'ADD_TO_CART' | 'PURCHASE';
  pageType: 'HOME' | 'CATEGORY' | 'PRODUCT_DETAIL' | 'CART' | 'CHECKOUT' | 'PURCHASE' | 'COMMON';
  url: string;                       // Request URL path (e.g., "/app/event/103291")
  sessionId: string;                 // Client session tracker UUID
  userId: string;                    // Client cookie tracking ID
  elementId?: string;                // Element ID for CLICK actions (e.g., "download-coupon-btn")
  extra?: {
    exhibitionId?: string;           // Extracted/Attributed Campaign ID
    exhibitionTitle?: string;        // Extracted/Attributed Campaign Title
    productId?: string;              // Product ID for cart/detail actions
    price?: number;                  // Single item price in KRW
    revenue?: number;                // Attributed transaction revenue in KRW
    orderId?: string;                // E-commerce purchase transaction ID
    attributedExhibitionId?: string; // Last-Touch Attributed Campaign ID for purchases
  }
}
```

### 3. Crucial Development & Maintenance Rules (Strictly Enforced)
- **NO Local Disk Write Policies**: Do NOT write analytical logs to serverless local directories (like `db_store/` or `/tmp`) via `fs.appendFile` or `fs.writeFile` in production serverless environments. Any local writes will be permanently destroyed when Vercel scales down or redeploys.
- **Hybrid In-Memory Caching Pattern (Performance)**:
  - ALWAYS preheat and keep the `globalEventsCache` hot in `server.js`.
  - **READ**: On `/api/stats`, return the memory cache `globalEventsCache` immediately to prevent gateway timeouts.
  - **WRITE**: On `/api/collect`, append the new event into the `globalEventsCache` synchronously, then push the synced array to `KV_STORE_URL` asynchronously without `await` to maintain high API responsiveness.
- **Self-Healing Fallback Seeding**: If the cloud database is wiped (e.g., via `/api/reset`) or returns an empty array, the server must automatically self-heal by calling `seedServerDatabase()` to restore a rich 5-day historic dataset, write it back to the cloud, and populate the memory cache.
- **Attribution Compute Model**: All daily performance metrics, stay durations, clicks, and revenue metrics must be computed dynamically on-the-fly by parsing the entire chronological event list. Do not rely on static predefined databases.
